WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.336
- All right, before we go

00:00:01.336 --> 00:00:03.240
I have one more tidbit
of joy I need to share.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.528
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:04.528 --> 00:00:05.837
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.837 --> 00:00:07.950
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.820
A sophomore at Reinhardt University,

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.210
just north of Atlanta,

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.810
is living out a dream, she
never even knew she had.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.970
She's a beloved player
on the woman's golf team,

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.650
and at 63 years old,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.190
one of the nation's
oldest student athletes.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.600
This year, she was even
nominated for homecoming court,

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.445
which is awesome.

00:00:23.445 --> 00:00:25.670
We have this truly remarkable woman

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:26.503
on the line now,

00:00:26.503 --> 00:00:28.590
watching on WSB-TV in Atlanta.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.515
Let's say hello to Debbie y'all.

00:00:30.515 --> 00:00:31.845
(audience cheering)

00:00:31.845 --> 00:00:32.772
- [Kelly] Hi Debbie.

00:00:32.772 --> 00:00:35.420
- Hi Kelly, thanks for inviting me.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.570
- Oh my Gosh, I'm so
stoked to have you on here.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.620
I love this.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.960
So, what made you decide
to go back to college,

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:41.793
in your sixties?

00:00:41.793 --> 00:00:42.870
That's so cool.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.670
- Well, I actually thought about college

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.830
when I was in high school,

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:49.830
and my guidance counselor
suggested Reinhardt back in 1976,

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:52.690
but my parents suggested X-ray school,

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.430
so that I'd always have
something to fall back on,

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:55.670
could always support myself.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:56.503
So I did.

00:00:56.503 --> 00:00:59.890
So I worked in X-ray then
taught skiing for 35 years.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:02.060
In my early thirties, I married my husband

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:03.610
and took up golf with him.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.710
His mother had been a
Dorm Mother at Reinhardt.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.770
And we had a great life.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.061
I was a housewife, had a ball
playing golf with my friends.

00:01:10.061 --> 00:01:12.730
And then four years ago he passed away.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.770
So I was a little lost in my golf.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:17.210
And I still continued to
play with my girlfriends,

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.140
and had a caddy at my club
in Atlanta one day, who said

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.050
he was a student on the
Reinhardt University golf team.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:28.470
So, I started thinking college is calling

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:29.710
and I looked into it.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:34.450
I called, emailed the
coach, went for a tryout.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.180
He said, yes, I could do it at my age.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.885
So I applied to school

00:01:37.885 --> 00:01:41.780
and went on first as a
walk on, on the team.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.120
And then, after my first year,

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.610
I was offered a scholarship,

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:47.730
partial scholarship.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.050
So we had Signing Day,

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.806
like everybody does with their parents.

00:01:50.806 --> 00:01:51.639
(audience laughing)

00:01:51.639 --> 00:01:53.240
- [Debbie] And my mom came to the library,

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.777
and we did Signing Day together,

00:01:55.777 --> 00:01:58.210
just like the real college kids do.

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:00.080
- [Kelly] I love it. Oh my gosh.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.020
It's so cool. I literally, this,

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.090
I'm not just saying this.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.680
I literally have told people, I'm like,

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:05.880
I want to do college when I'm older

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:07.060
and do all these things
that I always wanted to do

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:07.893
that I missed out on.

00:02:07.893 --> 00:02:09.750
Cause I, I ended up in the industry first.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:12.400
- [Kelly] And I feel like I
missed out on it. It's so cool.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.280
It's such a great story

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.580
because you're inspiring so many

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.270
people that still might want to do it.

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:18.140
And it's like literally never too late.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:21.100
- [Kelly] I think it was meant
to be with Reinhardt, right?

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:24.110
Like it just kept popping up
in your life at random points.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.990
So how is, how is college
life treating you now?

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:28.033
Are you partying?

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:30.783
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.740
- College life is awesome.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.650
This is my first semester
on campus because of COVID.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:38.483
- [Debbie] Where, I was virtual.

00:02:38.483 --> 00:02:41.130
- [Debbie] So now I'm meeting
my virtual classmates.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.760
- [Debbie] They're in my real classes now.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:43.880
And as a college athlete,

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.900
I have to take a full load to be eligible.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.840
So I'm taking Freshman PE, Statistics,

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.760
and some other classes
that can be really hard,

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.849
but I might get a 4.0
average I'm so surprised.

00:02:55.849 --> 00:02:57.303
- [Debbie] And just to go around campus

00:02:57.303 --> 00:02:58.530
with my teammates,

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.140
and see them off the golf course,

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.140
I see them at campus.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.030
- [Debbie] Then we go
to practice afterwards,

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.550
we're in the team-van together,

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:07.280
and I'm just having a ball, loving life.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.070
- [Debbie] They, I did have
to as far as the party thing.

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:12.570
I had to tell them, I may be
the 'old buddy' on the team,

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:15.200
but I cannot be the 'booze
buying buddy' on the team.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.410
- [Debbie] So they've accepted that.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.240
- [Debbie] I said it
could get me in trouble,

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.059
and I'm on track to graduate in 2023.

00:03:21.059 --> 00:03:22.121
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:03:22.121 --> 00:03:22.990
- [Debbie] And then I will buy the wine.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:24.530
Cause we will have a big party,

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.060
because five of my teammates

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.670
will graduate with me.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:30.209
And we will invite you to our graduation.

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:31.042
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:03:31.042 --> 00:03:35.100
- I think you're just about
the coolest frickin person

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:35.970
I've ever met.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.360
- [Kelly] I cannot wait
to meet you in person

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.193
and hug you.

00:03:38.193 --> 00:03:40.490
Literally, this is like my
dream in my sixties to do .

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.410
I'm not, I'm not lying.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:42.243
I've literally said,

00:03:42.243 --> 00:03:43.630
this is what I want to do when I retire.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:44.800
Cause I just think it's so cool.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.850
And if you feel like you missed out on it,

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:48.580
it's never too late to like

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.089
accomplish something you want to do.

00:03:50.089 --> 00:03:50.922
- [Debbie] Never too late.

00:03:50.922 --> 00:03:52.260
- [Kelly] And it's such,
it's such a great story

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.310
and I love you, Debbie.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:54.143
Thank you so much.

00:03:54.143 --> 00:03:55.809
- [Kelly] I'm liking your
post right now. All right.

00:03:55.809 --> 00:03:58.019
- [Debbie] Thank you so much.

00:03:58.019 --> 00:03:59.280
- [Kelly] All right, well that's not all.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.670
Our seasonal partner, Pilot,

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.290
the maker of 'FriXion',

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.410
the go-to erasable pen of
The Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.490
want to celebrate those creating
fearlessly, just like you.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.360
So they're going to give
you a thousand dollars.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:11.233
That'll help for college.

00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:13.702
- [Debbie] Oh, the team would love that.

00:04:13.702 --> 00:04:16.052
- [Kelly] That'll give
some books or something.

